        "raw": "<p>Legacy&#39;s bio does conspicuously mention that the WWII-era Legacy had a child very late in life. To me, that indicates that Finest Legacy probably began in the 70s in which case he was more realistically born in the late 40s or 50s to the previous Legacy, but <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ComicBookTime\">Comic Book Time</a> hit and, as he was the current and popular Legacy, he kept being &quot;in his 40s&quot; for a long time, with the occasional reboot making the WWII-era Legacy keep having a kid later and later in life. Not unlike how Marvel just keeps bumping back when Steve Rogers got thawed, or has to age-down Magneto occasionally to keep his Holocaust-survivor backstory.</p>",
